<title>UK: Norway's Gullfaks Nov loadings up 10 at 20 cargoes.</title>
<headline>Norway's Gullfaks Nov loadings up 10 at 20 cargoes.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-10-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>Norway's Gullfaks crude system is scheduled to load 20 cargoes in November, 10 more than the October programme which was cut by extensive scheduled maintenance work, traders said on Tuesday.  </p>
<p>Operator Statoil said on Friday Gullfaks production was stopping to allow annual maintenance to take place.</p>
<p>Gullfaks maintenance takes out about 500,000 barrels per day from Norwegian output, including 75,000 bpd from Saga Petroleum's Tordis field.</p>
<p>Gullfaks platforms are scheduled to resume production on October 24-25 while Tordis maintenance is expected to last until October 28.</p>
<p>Gullfaks crude loads offshore in 855,000-barrel cargoes.</p>
<p>-- Mark Thompson, London Newsroom +44 171 542 7930</p>
